{
  "schema": 29,
  "id": "buffered-bypass-3pdt-v1",
  "name": "Bypass · buffered (JFET buffer + 3PDT)",
  "version": {
    "major": 1,
    "minor": 2
  },
  "description": "The JFET source follower in front of a true-bypass 3PDT footswitch: the guitar always drives the buffer's high input impedance, on and bypassed, so a long cable after the pedal doesn't dull it. On: the buffer feeds your circuit (send) and its output (return) goes to the jack (out), the LED lit; bypassed: the buffer goes straight to out, your circuit's input grounded. The buffer's values are the JFET source follower block's starting values; the switching as in the True bypass block (Coda Effects, General Guitar Gadgets). Flip it in Knobs: Bypass.",
  "tags": [
    "bypass",
    "buffer",
    "footswitch",
    "switching",
    "jfet"
  ],
